WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.266
As Ash follows his dream to enter the Kalos League,

2
00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:08.866
our heroes continue toward Shalour City and Ash’s third Kalos Gym battle.

3
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:10.433
Na-na-na!

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.166
Ow! Dumb hair!

5
00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:16.233
- Is everyone ready?
- Pika.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.700
Bonnie, how about you?

7
00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:22.466
No, no, no. My hair won’t behave and I’m going crazy!

8
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:23.966
Na-na!

9
00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:27.200
- Let me give it a try.
- Uh, sure.

10
00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:30.799
Why don’t we do something different for a change?

11
00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:33.699
Huh? Different?

12
00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:37.199
- Do you like it?
- It’s so cute.

13
00:00:37.266 --> 00:00:40.666
It’s like a flower. I think it’s awesome.

14
00:00:45.766 --> 00:00:47.266
- Huh?
- Na-na?

15
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.633
Is that a Pokémon?

16
00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:51.000
Wow, it’s so cute!

17
00:00:51.066 --> 00:00:52.566
- What is?
- Pika?

18
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:54.866
- Isn’t that Pokémon...
- Let’s see.

19
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.966
Flabébé, the Single Bloom Pokémon.

20
00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:02.466
Flabébé chooses a favorite flower at the beginning of its life

21
00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:04.633
and takes care of it from then on.

22
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.366
But it doesn’t look like this Flabébé has a flower.

23
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:10.966
Not only that, it doesn’t look very happy.

24
00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.333
Maybe it’s hungry or something.

25
00:01:13.399 --> 00:01:15.366
Can we give it something to eat?

26
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:18.033
I have some flower nectar for Poké Puffs, see?

27
00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.500
Great. Here. It might be easiest to use this eyedropper to feed it.

28
00:01:22.566 --> 00:01:25.266
Yay. I want to do it, please!

29
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:29.800
Hang on a sec. Here you go. It’s sweet.

30
00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:34.633
Flabébé’s drinking it.

31
00:01:34.699 --> 00:01:37.633
It’s strange that it doesn’t have its own flower.

32
00:01:37.699 --> 00:01:41.633
And I’m wondering why that Flabébé landed in Bonnie’s hair.

33
00:01:41.699 --> 00:01:46.800
Oh, that’s easy, because my hair’s as beautiful as a flower, thanks to Serena.

34
00:01:46.866 --> 00:01:48.866
-Na-na-na!

35
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:52.300
Am I really that pretty?

36
00:01:52.366 --> 00:01:54.366
All right, I guess I am!

37
00:01:54.433 --> 00:01:56.899
Clemont, can you keep Flabébé for me?

38
00:01:56.966 --> 00:02:00.399
Oh, please, won’t you catch it for me, won’t you, please?

39
00:02:00.466 --> 00:02:03.600
I guess so. It seems to like you a lot, Bonnie.

40
00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:06.500
- All right. Flabébé, here goes.
- Flabé!

41
00:02:06.566 --> 00:02:09.333
- Huh? It didn’t work.
- Hm?

42
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.500
Is there something wrong, Flabébé?

43
00:02:11.566 --> 00:02:13.299
Bébé!

44
00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.666
It’s shaking its head.

45
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:18.866
You know, I’ll bet that Flabébé already has a Trainer.

46
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:21.233
Come on, no way! It can’t be!

47
00:02:21.299 --> 00:02:24.933
Flabébé’s my friend and that’s the way it is!

48
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.000
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

49
00:02:28.066 --> 00:02:31.433
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

50
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.266
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

51
00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:37.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

52
00:02:37.299 --> 00:02:40.299
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

53
00:02:40.366 --> 00:02:43.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

54
00:02:43.566 --> 00:02:46.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

55
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

56
00:02:49.433 --> 00:02:51.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

57
00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:54.900
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

58
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.100
Let’s go see Nurse Joy.

59
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:08.966
Maybe she can tell us something about Flabébé’s Trainer.

60
00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.966
I don’t want to say goodbye to Flabébé.

61
00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:15.000
I want you and I to always be together, okay?

62
00:03:15.066 --> 00:03:16.399
Flabé!

63
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.466
Flabébé.

64
00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:26.799
- Huh?
- Oh! It’s you. Flabébé.

65
00:03:26.866 --> 00:03:30.299
- Thank goodness you’re okay.
- Owie. You’re squishing me.

66
00:03:30.366 --> 00:03:33.233
Oh! Please forgive me. Huh?

67
00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:36.766
Flabébé? Won’t you come here?

68
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:40.333
- So is this man your Trainer, Flabébé?
- Bé.

69
00:03:40.399 --> 00:03:41.733
What’s wrong?

70
00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:46.233
- Maybe we should all say hi.
- Huh? I’m so sorry.

71
00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:48.233
Hello. My name is Grey.

72
00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:49.933
Hi. My name’s Ash.

73
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.600
- And this is my partner Pikachu.
- Pikachu.

74
00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:54.966
- I’m Clemont.
- I’m Serena.

75
00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.799
Bonnie's my name.

76
00:03:56.866 --> 00:03:59.466
- And this is Dedenne.
- Na-na!

77
00:03:59.533 --> 00:04:04.533
Thank you for taking care of my Flabébé. I’m grateful to you all.

78
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.566
All right, shall we go home, Flabébé?

79
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:10.266
- Fla!
- Huh?

80
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:13.466
I think Flabébé’s gotten quite attached to Bonnie’s hair.

81
00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:15.333
It doesn’t seem to want to leave.

82
00:04:15.399 --> 00:04:17.933
I think Flabébé really likes Bonnie, too.

83
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.266
If I may, I’m wondering why Flabébé doesn’t have a flower of its own.

84
00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:24.033
Well, it used to have one.

85
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.599
It was just the three of us living together,

86
00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:33.500
my wife, Florence, Flabébé, and me.

87
00:04:33.566 --> 00:04:38.266
Florence really loved and cherished Flabébé with all her heart.

88
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.233
Flabé!

89
00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.400
Bé! Bébé!

90
00:04:46.466 --> 00:04:50.133
What’s wrong? Florence. All you all right?

91
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.599
Bébé! Bébé!

92
00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:56.400
Florence had suddenly fallen ill. I immediately called for an ambulance

93
00:04:56.466 --> 00:05:00.200
and she was rushed to Calanthe Town Central Hospital.

94
00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:05.900
Florence will be in the hospital for quite a while.

95
00:05:05.966 --> 00:05:07.933
Bébé!

96
00:05:16.599 --> 00:05:19.966
When I awoke the next morning, Flabébé was gone.

97
00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:23.300
I thought it might have gone to the hospital to see Florence,

98
00:05:23.366 --> 00:05:25.800
so I hurried there to find out.

99
00:05:25.866 --> 00:05:29.000
When I got there, I found Flabébé in the rain,

100
00:05:29.066 --> 00:05:32.200
gazing at Florence through her hospital room window.

101
00:05:32.266 --> 00:05:35.766
It had a very worried expression on its face.

102
00:05:44.933 --> 00:05:46.366
Ah! Flabébé!

103
00:05:47.566 --> 00:05:49.666
Flab! Flabé!

104
00:05:49.733 --> 00:05:51.733
No. Flabébé, wait!

105
00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.266
Flabébé, come back!

106
00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.900
And I’ve been searching for Flabébé ever since

107
00:06:02.966 --> 00:06:06.266
and now Flabébé and I are finally reunited.

108
00:06:06.333 --> 00:06:10.266
- Flabébé, so that’s what happened?
- Bé.

109
00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:15.333
Of course. Now it makes sense to me why Flabébé flew to us without a flower.

110
00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:18.766
I’m afraid I have to bring Flabébé back with me right away.

111
00:06:18.833 --> 00:06:21.500
- Huh?
- Is something wrong?

112
00:06:21.566 --> 00:06:24.566
The doctor called and told me that Florence was all finished

113
00:06:24.633 --> 00:06:29.033
with her treatment, but still she wasn’t back to her normal, happy self.

114
00:06:29.099 --> 00:06:30.099
Oh, no!

115
00:06:30.166 --> 00:06:34.900
He said it’s not because of her illness but more of an emotional issue.

116
00:06:34.966 --> 00:06:37.333
I see. An emotional issue.

117
00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.666
I’ve got to bring Flabébé back to the hospital with me

118
00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.599
to see her as soon as I can.

119
00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:46.700
With one look, I’m sure Florence will start to feel like herself again.

120
00:06:46.766 --> 00:06:50.599
- So then, I guess you’d better hurry.
- Flabé.

121
00:06:50.666 --> 00:06:55.366
But without its flower, I’m afraid Flabébé will to start to grow weaker and weaker.

122
00:06:55.433 --> 00:06:56.333
Huh?

123
00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:01.433
So the first thing we need to do is find Flabébé’s flower as quickly as we can.

124
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.000
Huh, wait, why don’t we give Flabébé one of those flowers?

125
00:07:06.166 --> 00:07:08.700
A different flower won’t do us any good.

126
00:07:08.766 --> 00:07:12.000
You see, a Flabébé chooses the kind of flower it likes

127
00:07:12.066 --> 00:07:14.599
when it’s very young and stays with it forever

128
00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:18.333
and no other kind of flower will ever be able to replace it.

129
00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.866
Then let’s find the same kind of flower.

130
00:07:20.933 --> 00:07:25.466
Yeah, I’ll just go to a flower shop. So, what kind of flower is it?

131
00:07:25.533 --> 00:07:28.733
That’s very kind of you to offer your assistance.

132
00:07:28.799 --> 00:07:31.099
But its flower is a Fairy Flower

133
00:07:31.166 --> 00:07:33.700
and they don’t have them at a normal flower shop.

134
00:07:33.766 --> 00:07:35.433
Oh, man!

135
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.833
Pikachu!

136
00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.933
So, Fairy Flower, huh?

137
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.133
I know I’ve seen this flower somewhere.

138
00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.433
- On Bonnie’s head!
- Huh? Yeah, you’re right.

139
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.166
I see. The reason Flabébé landed on Bonnie’s head

140
00:07:50.233 --> 00:07:54.433
wasn’t because she looked pretty. It thought it saw its favorite flower.

141
00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:58.366
That makes sense. It’s always better using scientific reasoning.

142
00:07:58.433 --> 00:07:59.933
Why you... Oh!

143
00:08:00.066 --> 00:08:03.799
I want both Florence and Flabébé to get better but what to do?

144
00:08:03.866 --> 00:08:05.633
I guess I’m at a loss.

145
00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.566
I’ve got it. We’ll go and find a Fairy Flower.

146
00:08:08.633 --> 00:08:09.633
- Huh?
- Pika!

147
00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.299
In the meantime, you can go to the hospital

148
00:08:12.366 --> 00:08:14.033
and spend some time with Florence.

149
00:08:14.099 --> 00:08:17.766
Once we’ve located it, we’ll bring the flower over to you right away.

150
00:08:17.833 --> 00:08:19.466
I don’t know what to say.

151
00:08:19.533 --> 00:08:21.533
- I’ll look for it, too.
- Na-na!

152
00:08:21.599 --> 00:08:23.066
That would be wonderful.

153
00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:25.266
- Thank you all so much.
- Sure.

154
00:08:27.099 --> 00:08:30.766
- Flabébé, isn’t that nice?
- Flabé.

155
00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.233
Thank you once again.

156
00:08:34.299 --> 00:08:36.766
You can count on us.

157
00:08:36.833 --> 00:08:39.866
I think that Flabébé needs to feel better first.

158
00:08:39.933 --> 00:08:43.066
- So, let's go see Nurse Joy.
- Right.

159
00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.699
Flabébé’s all ready now.

160
00:08:52.766 --> 00:08:54.300
- Flabébé.
- Na-na!

161
00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:58.033
- I’m so glad you’re all right.
- For the time being.

162
00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:02.566
You see, Flabébé uses the energy of its flower to replenish its strength.

163
00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:08.600
And that’s why we’ve got to get out there and find a Fairy Flower as soon as we can.

164
00:09:08.666 --> 00:09:10.966
Do you know where Fairy Flowers grow?

165
00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:15.400
Let’s see. You should find Fairy Flowers growing in a field close to town.

166
00:09:15.466 --> 00:09:17.466
Yes, right here.

167
00:09:17.533 --> 00:09:21.833
One thing. Unfortunately, they’re out of season at the moment.

168
00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.699
It might be hard to find one.

169
00:09:24.766 --> 00:09:26.033
We’ll give it a shot.

170
00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.199
- Thank you, Nurse Joy.
- Pika.

171
00:09:28.266 --> 00:09:31.933
All right. Let’s go before Flabébé feels weak again.

172
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.800
- Come on.
- Right. Let’s hurry.

173
00:09:37.199 --> 00:09:42.300
Well, well, well, it seems we’ve been presented with a blooming opportunity.

174
00:09:42.366 --> 00:09:44.000
What next?

175
00:09:44.066 --> 00:09:47.066
First we plant the seed, then water it, then bam!

176
00:09:47.133 --> 00:09:48.300
Yes, ma’am!

177
00:09:49.533 --> 00:09:53.800
Whoa! Which way is the field where the Fairy Flowers grow?

178
00:09:53.866 --> 00:09:54.766
Pikachu!

179
00:09:54.833 --> 00:09:57.300
- It looks like we go straight this way.
- Great.

180
00:09:57.366 --> 00:10:00.366
I calculate we’ll be there in approximately an hour.

181
00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:03.300
- Won’t be long. You’ll be fine.
- Na-na!

182
00:10:03.366 --> 00:10:05.666
Welcome, don’t ya know, ya!

183
00:10:05.733 --> 00:10:08.233
We’re here to take you on a happy-go-lucky tour

184
00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:11.866
of the lovely surroundings nature has to offer, ya, don’t ya know.

185
00:10:11.933 --> 00:10:15.533
If you’re looking for Fairy Flowers, we’ll help you find them, don’t ya know.

186
00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.433
You’ll help us find a Fairy Flower?

187
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:21.500
Maybe two, don’t ya know. Since they’re out of season at the moment,

188
00:10:21.566 --> 00:10:24.500
an amateur would have a hard time finding one, don’t ya know.

189
00:10:24.566 --> 00:10:26.900
Nurse Joy did tell us the same thing.

190
00:10:26.966 --> 00:10:30.100
But wait! There’s more. Today’s your lucky day.

191
00:10:30.166 --> 00:10:33.733
Our first four customers get their tour for free, don’t ya know, ya!

192
00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:35.433
- Huh?
- Wow. You mean it?

193
00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.266
We’ve never been meaner.

194
00:10:37.333 --> 00:10:39.733
It is our lucky day.

195
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.100
Come on. We don’t have that much time.

196
00:10:42.166 --> 00:10:45.100
Let’s go with them so we can find a Fairy Flower.

197
00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:46.966
- Pika, Pika!
- Don’t ya know.

198
00:10:47.033 --> 00:10:49.033
Clemont, you’re starting to talk like them.

199
00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.333
Oh, sorry.

200
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.766
Oh, ya. I want to thank you fine folks for participating

201
00:10:53.833 --> 00:10:57.199
in our special free-for-all happy-go-lucky tour, don’t ya know.

202
00:10:57.266 --> 00:11:01.433
I say we get this trappy-go-twerpy tour off and touring, don’t ya know, ya.

203
00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.800
- Huh?
- He forgot his brain, ya.

204
00:11:03.866 --> 00:11:06.533
Okay, right this way, don’t ya know, ya.

205
00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:14.199
We’re here, ya! Fairy Flowerland, don’t cha know.

206
00:11:14.266 --> 00:11:16.733
Ah, I can’t believe how fast we got here.

207
00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.933
You’re guided by great guides, don’t ya know.

208
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.166
Without us, you’d be walking in circles, ya.

209
00:11:23.233 --> 00:11:27.199
- Not so sure about that.
- We’ve been on this path the whole time.

210
00:11:27.266 --> 00:11:30.400
Listen, what’s important now is that we find a Fairy Flower.

211
00:11:30.466 --> 00:11:32.933
Yeah, Grey’s waiting for us at the hospital.

212
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.666
- All right, Bonnie. Ready?
- Huh? Mm.

213
00:11:36.733 --> 00:11:42.166
Flabébé? I promise we’re going to find just the kind of flower you like, okay?

214
00:11:42.233 --> 00:11:43.966
I don’t want to say goodbye,

215
00:11:44.033 --> 00:11:48.133
but there’s somebody special waiting for you who needs you.

216
00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.400
I’m not finding any Fairy Flowers.

217
00:11:51.466 --> 00:11:54.600
Me neither. It looks like Nurse Joy was right on the mark

218
00:11:54.666 --> 00:11:56.600
when she said that they’re now out of season.

219
00:11:56.666 --> 00:11:58.633
- I’m getting worried.
- Hm.

220
00:11:58.699 --> 00:12:02.433
- What’s the deal? I don’t see any either.
- Pikachu!

221
00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.466
You’re our tour guides. Can’t you do something?.

222
00:12:05.533 --> 00:12:09.199
But of course. You leave things to us, don’t ya know, ya.

223
00:12:09.266 --> 00:12:12.500
Fairy Flower, Fairy Flower, show yer pretty face, ya.

224
00:12:12.566 --> 00:12:14.966
There must be a Fairy Flower around this place, ya.

225
00:12:15.033 --> 00:12:17.500
Man. They’re no help at all.

226
00:12:20.466 --> 00:12:22.633
Hey, what is it?

227
00:12:22.699 --> 00:12:24.866
Ah! Look.

228
00:12:24.933 --> 00:12:31.000
I think that’s a Fairy Flower and it’s blooming way up on that cliff over there!

229
00:12:31.066 --> 00:12:34.033
- That’s it, all right.
- Yes! Let’s go.

230
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.199
Who’s that Pokémon?

231
00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.500
It’s Flabébé.

232
00:13:01.966 --> 00:13:03.966
See? It’s right up there.

233
00:13:04.033 --> 00:13:05.533
Flabé.

234
00:13:05.599 --> 00:13:09.699
I don’t think Flabébé’s strong enough to fly all the way up there by itself.

235
00:13:09.766 --> 00:13:11.533
I’ll go and get it.

236
00:13:11.599 --> 00:13:14.300
- Ash! You can’t pull it up.
- Huh?

237
00:13:14.366 --> 00:13:19.300
Flabébé needs to grab onto a flower that’s still growing naturally out of the ground.

238
00:13:19.366 --> 00:13:24.199
Huh? Okay. Then I’ll bring Flabébé up there with me.

239
00:13:24.266 --> 00:13:28.300
- If I take you, you can get your flower.
- Flabé!

240
00:13:28.366 --> 00:13:30.900
- Uh...
- It’s too dangerous, Bonnie.

241
00:13:30.966 --> 00:13:34.933
It’ll be all right. I’m way better at climbing than you are, hm!

242
00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.199
- Oh, Bonnie.
- Na-na!

243
00:13:37.266 --> 00:13:39.699
- Be careful.
- You can do it.

244
00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:49.400
Pika, Pika!

245
00:13:49.466 --> 00:13:53.033
Ah! Huh!

246
00:14:01.966 --> 00:14:03.466
A little more.

247
00:14:03.533 --> 00:14:06.400
There’s no distraction like twerp distraction.

248
00:14:06.466 --> 00:14:08.199
Pikachu catching time.

249
00:14:08.266 --> 00:14:12.266
- I’m all over it. Ya!
- Pika?

250
00:14:17.766 --> 00:14:21.566
Flabébé, we made it up. See? There’s the Fairy Flower.

251
00:14:21.633 --> 00:14:24.933
Flabébé!

252
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.866
Oh, wow!

253
00:14:26.933 --> 00:14:28.966
Flabébé grabbed onto the Fairy Flower.

254
00:14:29.033 --> 00:14:31.400
- All right!
- Bonnie, you were amazing.

255
00:14:31.466 --> 00:14:32.800
- Na-na!
- Pika, Pika!

256
00:14:32.866 --> 00:14:35.366
- Huh?
- Pikachu!

257
00:14:35.433 --> 00:14:37.366
- Pikachu.
- Huh?

258
00:14:37.433 --> 00:14:40.300
All right! What are you doing with Pikachu?

259
00:14:42.166 --> 00:14:44.699
Prepare for trouble, things are all right.

260
00:14:44.766 --> 00:14:47.099
'Cause catching Pikachu makes our world bright.

261
00:14:47.166 --> 00:14:49.599
To protect the world from devastation.

262
00:14:49.666 --> 00:14:52.333
To unite all people within our nation.

263
00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:55.266
To denounce the evils of truth and love.

264
00:14:55.333 --> 00:14:58.099
To extend our reach to the stars above.

265
00:14:58.166 --> 00:15:00.733
- Jessie!
- And James!

266
00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:03.699
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

267
00:15:03.766 --> 00:15:06.900
Surrender now or prepare for one fine flowery fight.

268
00:15:06.966 --> 00:15:10.333
- Meowth, that’s right.
- Wobbuffet!

269
00:15:12.833 --> 00:15:15.966
Team Rocket. I should have known it was you.

270
00:15:16.033 --> 00:15:18.900
So should I! But soon, it's not going to matter.

271
00:15:18.966 --> 00:15:22.266
- Wow. Those guys make me so mad.
- Flabé!

272
00:15:22.333 --> 00:15:24.166
Teach them a lesson, guys.

273
00:15:24.233 --> 00:15:25.766
- Froakie!
- Fennekin!

274
00:15:25.833 --> 00:15:27.466
Chespin!

275
00:15:29.066 --> 00:15:31.733
All right, Pumpkaboo, out!

276
00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:34.900
Okay, Inkay, what do you say?

277
00:15:37.566 --> 00:15:39.733
Froakie, use Water Pulse.

278
00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.099
Froakie!

279
00:15:42.166 --> 00:15:45.466
- Now, spoil their fun.
- Wobbuff!

280
00:15:45.533 --> 00:15:47.733
Froakie!

281
00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.199
- Froakie!
- Fennekin!

282
00:15:49.266 --> 00:15:52.866
- Now, Chespin, Pin Missile, let’s go!
- Chespin!

283
00:15:52.933 --> 00:15:56.866
- Spoil their fun once more.
- Wobbuff!

284
00:15:59.433 --> 00:16:03.133
- Inkay, Psybeam!
- Inkay!

285
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:08.633
Shadow Ball!

286
00:16:08.699 --> 00:16:12.000
All right, dodge it.

287
00:16:12.066 --> 00:16:15.500
Oh, now, what are we all going to do?

288
00:16:15.566 --> 00:16:18.866
Flabé!

289
00:16:18.933 --> 00:16:21.300
Flabébé?

290
00:16:27.366 --> 00:16:30.800
- Flabébé.
- The Fairy Flower must have revived it.

291
00:16:30.866 --> 00:16:34.000
- Strange.
- What in the world?

292
00:16:34.066 --> 00:16:36.066
Oh!

293
00:16:36.133 --> 00:16:37.633
What a world.

294
00:16:37.699 --> 00:16:41.300
I’ve somehow achieved a contented and peaceful state.

295
00:16:41.366 --> 00:16:45.466
What’s up with you two? Let’s get the twerps off the grid.

296
00:16:45.533 --> 00:16:48.233
You needn’t be so angry, Meowth, old chum.

297
00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:51.300
He’s right. Fighting is so barbaric.

298
00:16:51.366 --> 00:16:54.500
- Relax.
- Give it a rest.

299
00:17:00.199 --> 00:17:03.500
Turn off your mind, relax and float downstream.

300
00:17:03.566 --> 00:17:06.300
So, what should we do now?

301
00:17:06.366 --> 00:17:09.266
Why don’t we set adorable little Pikachu free?

302
00:17:09.333 --> 00:17:11.500
That’s fine with me!

303
00:17:11.566 --> 00:17:15.500
- Off you go, little buddy.
- Pika!

304
00:17:15.566 --> 00:17:17.066
- Pikachu!
- Pika! Pi!

305
00:17:17.133 --> 00:17:21.500
I’m glad you’re back, but what’s gotten into Team Rocket anyway?

306
00:17:21.566 --> 00:17:24.466
Oh, I see. The pollen from Flabébé has the power

307
00:17:24.533 --> 00:17:26.833
to make everybody feel wonderfully relaxed.

308
00:17:26.899 --> 00:17:31.433
So when anyone acts aggressively towards it, it simply scatters its pollen.

309
00:17:32.566 --> 00:17:36.766
- Ah!
- Flabé!

310
00:17:36.833 --> 00:17:41.233
Flabébé! Thanks so much for everything.

311
00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:44.433
We’re fine 'cause of you.

312
00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.000
We should get going. Grey and Florence are waiting for us.

313
00:17:48.066 --> 00:17:51.133
- Pikachu!
- Ash is right. Let’s go fast.

314
00:18:04.066 --> 00:18:07.733
Ah! It’s a beautiful Team Rocket day.

315
00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.500
They’ll be back here soon.

316
00:18:17.566 --> 00:18:21.833
Ash and his friends were kind enough to look for another Fairy Flower for Flabébé.

317
00:18:21.899 --> 00:18:27.566
Oh, the trouble I’ve caused. I hope you’ll find it in your heart to forgive me.

318
00:18:29.866 --> 00:18:31.899
Come in.

319
00:18:31.966 --> 00:18:35.333
- Hi there, Grey. Sorry we took so long.
- Pikachu!

320
00:18:35.399 --> 00:18:37.700
But we finally found a Fairy Flower.

321
00:18:37.766 --> 00:18:40.300
Oh, that’s so wonderful to hear.

322
00:18:40.366 --> 00:18:42.833
- Now, Bonnie, please?
- Okay.

323
00:18:48.333 --> 00:18:49.933
Oh, Flabébé!

324
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.300
- Oh!
- Fla!

325
00:18:52.366 --> 00:18:54.566
Flabé! Fla!

326
00:18:54.633 --> 00:18:57.766
- I’m so happy to see you.
- Flabé!

327
00:18:57.833 --> 00:19:02.300
It’s simply amazing how much better I feel seeing you again.

328
00:19:02.366 --> 00:19:03.633
Fla!

329
00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:12.399
I can’t thank you enough for going to all the trouble of finding a Fairy Flower.

330
00:19:12.466 --> 00:19:15.966
That was so kind of you, dear Ash and Clemont and Serena,

331
00:19:16.033 --> 00:19:18.366
and little Bonnie, thank you all.

332
00:19:18.433 --> 00:19:21.566
- It was really all Bonnie’s work.
- Clemont’s right.

333
00:19:21.633 --> 00:19:24.300
The Fairy Flower was all the way up on a cliff

334
00:19:24.366 --> 00:19:27.366
and she climbed up there with Flabébé to get it.

335
00:19:27.433 --> 00:19:30.033
Bonnie, I am indeed grateful.

336
00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.733
And I am, too, dear.

337
00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:33.366
Thanks.

338
00:19:38.166 --> 00:19:39.633
Huh? Hi there!

339
00:19:41.933 --> 00:19:46.100
We only played for a short time, but it was a lot of fun.

340
00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:52.800
Now you can be with Grey and Florence. You take good care of them.

341
00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.899
Know what? I’ll see you.

342
00:19:58.966 --> 00:20:04.333
- Flabé! Flabé!
- Mm!

343
00:20:15.333 --> 00:20:17.200
Na-na?

344
00:20:18.866 --> 00:20:21.866
- Huh?
- Na-na! Na-na-na!

345
00:20:21.933 --> 00:20:26.466
Huh? You’re right, Dedenne. You’re here!

346
00:20:26.533 --> 00:20:27.533
Na-na!

347
00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.233
- Okay. Let’s go.
- Huh?

348
00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:30.200
Pikachu!

349
00:20:31.566 --> 00:20:33.866
Right!

350
00:20:33.933 --> 00:20:35.933
Thanks to Bonnie’s courage and caring,

351
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.466
Flabébé has a beautiful new Fairy Flower

352
00:20:38.533 --> 00:20:41.899
and Florence, Flabébé and Grey are together once again,

353
00:20:41.966 --> 00:20:45.800
as our heroes’ Kalos journey continues.
